# INSTALL manifest for the Angband App Store package (#gamedata2).
#
# WHY THIS PACKAGE EXISTS AT ALL. Angband's 1.4 MB lib data tree (gamedata,
# customize, help, screens: 69 files) used to live at "/ANGBAND/", and
# userland/libc/pkgdest.c permits a package destination ONLY under /APPS, /GAMES
# or /THEMES, so that root was REFUSED outright and the data had to be baked into
# every golden. The port now compiles with
# -DDEFAULT_CONFIG_PATH/-DDEFAULT_LIB_PATH="/GAMES/ANGBAND/lib/" and the whole
# payload is one TREE rule.
#
# See the AssaultCube package's INSTALL for the rule grammar and for why the
# min-client line is load-bearing rather than decorative.
#!mpkg-min-client 2
#
# The binary, from the same package as its data: shipping one without the other
# is exactly the #627 defect, and invariant-gate.sh check 14b now enforces the
# pair for this game the way check 14 does for AssaultCube.
ANGBAND -> /APPS/ANGBAND
#
# THE READ-ONLY LIB TREE. init_file_paths() (src/init.c) derives
# ANGBAND_DIR_GAMEDATA and ANGBAND_DIR_CUSTOMIZE from configpath and
# ANGBAND_DIR_HELP and ANGBAND_DIR_SCREENS from libpath; this port sets both
# macros to the same value, so all four land here.
#
# IT IS A "lib/" SUBDIRECTORY OF THE SAVE ROOT, NOT THE SAVE ROOT ITSELF, and
# there is no collision: Angband appends VERSION_NAME to PRIVATE_USER_PATH, so
# every WRITABLE directory sits under /GAMES/ANGBAND/Angband/{save,scores,panic,
# archive}, a differently-named sibling of lib/. Keeping them apart is what lets
# the installed payload stay read-only while the save tree stays writable, rather
# than intermixing a package's files with a player's.
#
# create_needed_dirs() (src/init.c) creates ONLY those five writable directories;
# its own comment says the data directories "are assumed to contain required files
# and therefore must exist at startup". So this tree is never created at run time:
# if the package does not put it here, the game quits before its first screen.
lib/ -> /GAMES/ANGBAND/lib/
